 "notes": "Section 7 (Eureka Valley, Castro, Mission, Buena Vista; joins Sec. 6 above, 12 left, 2 right, 8 below as scanned), 1-bit photocopy, 5400x4124, the sheet lies on its side (title reads top to bottom). Page turned ~0.55 deg (left rule x 305 at the top to 335 at the bottom; top rule y 345 at the left to 330 at the right). Frame on all four sides: thick bar (~15 px), ~5 px of white, thin inner rule (3-4 px, the innermost rule), with a thick + thin quarter arc (radius ~205-213 px) in every corner. The outline lies on paper 1-2 px inside the thin rule's inner edge (README rules 1, 8), points every <=60 px. Corners (rule 2): the outline follows the inner edge of the thin arc 1-2 px inside it; each thin arc's tail runs beside its side rule and joins it through a short connector, and the outline goes round tail and connector, so they and the gap between tail and rule are outside (TL: tail beside the left rule down to y 563, connector on the top rule at x 517-520; TR: connector at x 4844-4847 on the top rule and y 546-549 on the right rule; BL: y 3718-3721 on the left rule, x 551-553 on the bottom rule; BR: y 3718-3721 on the right rule, x 4857-4861 on the bottom rule). Kind (b), map ink that truly touches the frame and is left under the outline: the solid commercial blocks run into the left rule at y ~2000-2150, 2290-2350, 2740-3100 and 3440-3600 (nearly black stretches); the diagonal hatching of the first-residential area runs into the left rule (y ~560-1310), the TL arc and the top rule (x ~520-1500); solid blocks and street lines touch the top rule (x ~2540-2770 and elsewhere) and one block the bottom rule at x ~1350-1410; a hatch line meets the TL arc's connector on the top rule (x 520-527) and another the TL junction on the left rule (y 563-565), and the outline crosses them there. remove: (1) the rotated CITY & COUNTY OF SAN FRANCISCO / USE OF PROPERTY / ZONE MAP / CITY PLANNING COMMISSION title, LEGEND with its six swatches, and the SCALE bar with its lettering (top right, no ruled box, on open paper), an 11-point stepped outline ~4-6 px outside the ink: top edge just above the swatches (two street lines end 1 px above them), top-right corner cut off inside the TR arc, bottom edge in the 8 ink-free rows between LIGHT INDUSTRIAL DIST. and the block below, stepped up under UNRESTRICTED and the scale bar's 1000 so the blocks and park paths at the lower left stay map; (2) the compass rose with its three long arrows (tail feather at x 4320-4385, arrow tip at 5034,3771, second needle to 4991,3854): the rose stands on open paper but the long arrow's tail feather lies over the corner of a cross-hatched block and the block lines beside it, so the outline is drawn close round the arrows (19 points, ~6-10 px outside the ink) to leave the block's hatching as map; at the feather it crosses block ink (remove-outline ink ~57); (3) the SECTION 7 badge (ring centre 4965.1,3525.0, outer radius 56.9), an octagon 5 px outside the ring, on open paper. 'Join Sec.' lettering prints outside the frame. Doubt: a small squiggle at (4375-4388, 3730-3745) just under the tail feather is left as map (not clearly part of the compass).",
 "drawn_by": "Claude (training-label agent LA, issue #71), 2026-11-21: from the scan and inputs/frame-labels/README.md only (no model output looked at). Sides: inner edge of the innermost (thin) rule measured every 2nd px from luminance profiles (thin run beside the bar), robust local-linear fit, then each px of the outline re-set 2 px inside the rule's measured inner end where paper lies inside it (within 1.5 px of the fit; the fit kept where map ink is merged with the rule). Corner arcs: circle fitted to the arc band's inner edge along rays, plus the measured residual by angle; arc ends (stubs) hand-placed from pixel dumps. Remove blocks from full-resolution crops. Checked on straightened 3x/6x strips of the whole outline (every vertex), pixel dumps of all eight arc ends, and the ranked ink stretches."
